---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../../components/PageHero.astro";
import { sitePath } from "../../lib/paths";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How to use this site"
  description="A practical guide to reading Independent Observer publication records, status labels, sources, citations, revisions, and corrections."
  currentPath="/how-to-use-this-site/"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Reader guide"
    title="How to use this site"
    description="Use each public item as a record with a stated status, source boundary, revision trail, and route for correction."
  />
  <section class="section section-white">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>Start with the publication record</h2>
      <p>
        Public items carry a compact record identifying their status, author, available dates,
        version where recorded, revision history, reuse notice, and citation information. A record
        describes what a reader can rely on now; it does not turn a preview into peer-reviewed work.
      </p>
      <h2>Read the status before the argument</h2>
      <p>
        A concept preview, working paper, public reading copy, and published bounded adaptation do
        not carry the same release boundary. Read the <a
          href={sitePath("/governance/#status-labels")}>status-label definitions</a
        > before treating an item as a completed publication.
      </p>
      <h2>Follow sources and limitations</h2>
      <p>
        Source notes identify material used by the page where available. Limitations describe what
        the page does not establish. A linked source supports its own claim; it does not
        automatically validate every interpretation on the page that cites it.
      </p>
      <h2>Cite the public record accurately</h2>
      <p>
        Use the suggested citation or downloadable citation record only when the page provides the
        necessary author and date metadata. Cite the exact page and version you read. Do not present
        a site reading copy as an independently peer-reviewed publication unless the page says so.
      </p>
      <h2>Check revisions and corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Recorded paper corrections identify a date, change, reason, and affected section. The public
        <a href={sitePath("/latest/#latest-revisions-title")}>revision log</a> collects those entries;
        interface and software changes are listed separately in <a href={sitePath("/whats-new/")}
          >What’s New</a
        >.
      </p>
      <h2>Ask a question or suggest a correction</h2>
      <p>
        Use the <a href={sitePath("/contact/")}>contact page</a> and include the page address, the passage
        at issue, and supporting evidence. The site’s correction, privacy, disclosure, and reuse policies
        are stated on the <a href={sitePath("/governance/")}>governance page</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="reader-guide-next">
        <a class="button" href={sitePath("/latest/")}>See new and revised work →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .reader-guide-next {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
</style>
